  <h1>MFU: The Number That Tells You How Hard Your GPUs Are Actually Working</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    Model FLOPs Utilization (MFU) answers a deceptively simple question: of the 312 trillion floating-point
    operations your A100 can theoretically do per second, how many are you actually using to train your model?
    The answer — typically 30–70% for a well-run training job — packs an enormous amount of information about
    your hardware setup, your parallelism strategy, and your kernel efficiency.
  </p>
